{"kind":"request","text":"codex: measure the durable-append write path's git subprocess cost and propose a batching design for ratification — evidence and design only, no implementation in this lane. Sequence this after your backlog-disposition request 4b12b30f; it is not urgent relative to those merges.\n\nWHY. Every signed append runs a chain of git subprocesses and costs on the order of 170ms in tests on hugh's machine (measured 2026-09-01 at local main c3169d83); the same per-act cost is the floor under both the slow test gate (cmd/gs 476s, internal/app 216s, internal/kernel 206s of test wall time are dominated by workroom construction) and the long-standing slowness of local gs writes. Claude's test-infrastructure lane (my request 52be1b19) attacks the test-side cost with fsync-off fixtures and reuse; this lane is the deeper fix: fewer subprocesses per act in the production write path itself.\n\nASK. (1) Instrument or count the exact git invocations one append performs today (a PATH-shim subprocess count is the honest measure), broken down by phase — object writes, ref updates, reads. (2) Propose the remedy with numbers: candidates include batching object writes (hash-object --stdin-paths, cat-file --batch-command, or an in-process object writer), consolidating ref updates (update-ref --stdin), and eliminating redundant reads per act. State the expected per-append cost after, what durability or atomicity properties change and why they remain sound (the fold's authority and signature model must be untouched), and the test strategy. (3) File the design as a proposal for ratification before any implementation request. If you judge the write path already minimal or the win not worth the risk, report that with the measurements and I will retire this lane.","body":{"conditions":"A measured per-append git-subprocess accounting (counts by phase, not seconds alone) at a stated head; a written design proposing the batching remedy with expected costs, unchanged authority/signature and durability properties argued explicitly, and a test strategy, filed as a proposal for ratification before any implementation; or a measured report that the path is already minimal, upon which the author retires this request. No production code changes in this lane.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}